# ATO Lodgment BAS vs Biz Intel period

## Invariant

**ATO entry order** fields (G1, 1A, 1B, 1C/7C) are values to type into Online Services for **one BAS cycle** (usually one quarter). They must **not** equal Biz Intel when the P&L banner is **Financial Year** or another multi-quarter window.

Confirmed SELPIC example:

| Source | 1B | 1C (net) |
|--------|-----|----------|
| Biz Intel **FY** | ~$563.83 (Q3+Q4 claimable) | ~$747.03 |
| ATO lodge **Q4** | ~$545.38 | Q4-only 1A−1B |
| ATO lodge **Q3** | ~$18.45 (or already lodged / near-zero net after refund) | that quarter only |

Copying FY $747.03 into a quarterly BAS is wrong.

## Default lodging window

`resolveBasLodgmentQuarterForFiling`:

1. Banner is exact Q1–Q4 → that quarter  
2. Banner is FY / Full statement / custom → **BAS quarter of banner end date** (FY 30 Jun → **Q4**)  
3. Else density fallback  

Optional dropdown: “Biz Intel P&L only (do not lodge this sum)” for comparison — never the default.

## CTR / Annual

Still full FY (company tax / annual forms). Different from BAS.

## Do

- Match ATO entry to **selected BAS quarter** (and Biz Intel only when banner is that same quarter)
- Warn when Biz Intel is on FY while BAS tab shows Q4

## Do not

- Default ATO BAS fields to the full P&L / FY window  
- Treat FY GST Net as one quarterly remittance  
- Assume Q3 “0” on screen means Q3 1B was zero — check that quarter’s BAS (refund ≠ 1B)
